---
/**
 * The ORI7 / ORI9 explainer. The single most useful thing on this page: people
 * routinely hand over the seven-character form because a directory listed it
 * first, and the form is rejected. So the pair is presented as a comparison
 * with an explicit "use this one".
 */
---

<div class="ori-compare">
  <div class="ori-card anim-hard-left">
    <div class="ori-card-head">
      <h3>ORI7</h3>
      <span class="ori-badge">Short form</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ori-sample mono">NJ00101</div>
    <div class="ori-chars">Seven characters</div>
    <p>
      The compact form of the same identifier: the two-letter state code followed by the county and
      municipality digits. It names the exact same agency as the ORI9 — it is simply truncated.
    </p>
    <div class="ori-rule">
      <strong>When to use it</strong>
      Only when a form or portal explicitly asks for a seven-character ORI. If the field doesn't say,
      this is not the one.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ori-card is-standard anim-hard-right">
    <div class="ori-card-head">
      <h3>ORI9</h3>
      <span class="ori-badge use-this">Use this one</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ori-sample mono">NJ00101<span class="pad">00</span></div>
    <div class="ori-chars">Nine characters &mdash; ORI7 plus two padding characters</div>
    <p>
      The standard nine-character form, and what nearly every fingerprinting appointment, firearms
      application and background-check form expects. It is the ORI7 with two characters appended to
      fill the field.
    </p>
    <div class="ori-rule">
      <strong>When to use it</strong>
      By default. Give the ORI9 unless you are told, in writing, that seven characters are required.
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .ori-compare {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(320px, 100%), 1fr));
    gap: 25px;
    margin-bottom: 90px;
  }

  .ori-card {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-card);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 32px 30px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .ori-card.is-standard {
    border-top-color: var(--primary);
  }

  .ori-card-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .ori-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-bright);
    letter-spacing: 2px;
  }

  .ori-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 5px 11px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .ori-badge.use-this {
    color: var(--text-bright);
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary-edge);
  }

  .ori-sample {
    font-size: 2.1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 4px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    word-break: break-all;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .ori-sample .pad {
    color: var(--text-bright);
    background: rgba(155, 27, 27, 0.55);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 0 4px;
  }

  .ori-chars {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .ori-card p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .ori-rule {
    margin-top: auto;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    padding-top: 16px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-main);
  }

  .ori-rule strong {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .ori-sample {
      font-size: 1.6rem;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
    }
  }
</style>
